{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructureFeasibility","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructureFeasibility","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.exists_angleStructure_of_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.exists_angleStructure_of_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L173-L177","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructureFeasibilityContext.exists_angleStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructureFeasibilityContext.exists_angleStructure","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L171-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructureFeasibilityContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructureFeasibilityContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L170-L170","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructureFeasibilityContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructureFeasibilityContext","kind":"class","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L156-L171","doc":"**Sufficiency (HARD — OPEN in this file).** Rivin's existence theorem: a\nHall-type combinatorial-expansion condition on the incidence data forces a\nfeasible angle structure to *exist*. The hypothesis `hExp` asks that every\nnonempty vertex set `W` meet strictly more than `2 · |W|` edges — the discrete\nslack that a max-flow–min-cut / Hall argument turns into a strictly-interior\npoint of the angle-structure polytope.\n\nThis converse to the necessity lemmas above is the analytic core of Rivin's\ncombinatorial optimization and is **not proved here**: it is stated with an\nexplicit `sorry` and a bibliographic citation, per the repository's Lean\ndiscipline (an honest \"stated, not yet proved\" marker — no axiom, no fake\nclosure). This requires massive infrastructure (Hall / max-flow–min-cut analytic core)\nthat cannot be added as a simple class field, and is thus left as an explicit sorry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.angleStructure_cutset_gt_two_pi_imp_not_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.angleStructure_cutset_gt_two_pi_imp_not_star","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L139-L154","doc":"**Necessity — the cutset / separation condition.** Any edge set `S` whose\nangles exceed the full-turn budget `2 * pi` is **not** contained in a single\nvertex's star. Equivalently: a set of edges all incident to one vertex can never\nbe a nontrivial cutset, because its angle sum is at most `2 * pi`.\n\nThis is the easy direction of Rivin's cutset inequality — it *derives* the\n\"separating / not-all-at-one-vertex\" clause from the vertex turn conditions and\npositivity, rather than assuming it. Falsifiable: if `S ⊆ star v`, then\n`∑ e ∈ S, A e ≤ ∑ e ∈ star v, A e = 2 * pi`, contradicting `2 * pi < ∑ e ∈ S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.angleStructure_edge_lt_vertex_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.angleStructure_edge_lt_vertex_total","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L125-L137","doc":"**Necessity — an edge is below the vertex turn budget.** Every edge angle is\nstrictly less than the full turn `2 * pi` at any vertex it meets.\n\nFalsifiable: an edge angle `≥ 2 * pi` would, with the remaining strictly positive\nangles around the vertex, push the vertex sum above `2 * pi`, contradicting the\nturn condition. Here proved directly from `angle_lt_pi` and `pi < 2 * pi`\n(which needs `pi_pos`), so it uses the model's hypotheses and is not a\ntautology. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.angleStructure_vertex_min_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.angleStructure_vertex_min_degree","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L106-L123","doc":"**Necessity — vertex minimum degree.** In any feasible angle structure every\nvertex meets **at least three** edges.\n\nThis is genuinely falsifiable count bookkeeping: each incident angle is `< pi`,\nso a vertex with `k` incident edges has angle sum `< k · pi`; the turn condition\npins that sum at `2 · pi`, forcing `2 · pi < k · pi`, i.e. `k > 2`. A vertex with\none or two incident edges would violate the turn condition, so the model\nexcludes it. (Not a tautology: it uses `angle_lt_pi`, `pi_pos`, and `vertex`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.star_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.star_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L95-L104","doc":"The star of a vertex is nonempty: an empty star would give a vertex angle\nsum of `0`, contradicting the full-turn value `2 * pi > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.vertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.vertex","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The angles around every vertex sum to a full turn `2 * pi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.angle_lt_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.angle_lt_pi","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L89-L89","doc":"Each edge angle is strictly below a straight angle `pi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.angle_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.angle_pos","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L87-L87","doc":"Each edge angle is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.pi_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.pi_pos","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The straight-angle scalar is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.AngleStructure","kind":"structure","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/AngleStructureFeasibility.lean#L78-L91","doc":"An **angle structure** on the incidence data `star : V → Finset E`, valued in\nan ordered ring `R` with abstract straight-angle scalar `pi`. Each edge carries a\nstrictly positive angle below `pi`, and the angles around every vertex sum to a\nfull turn `2 * pi`. The cutset (separation) inequalities are *derived* from these\nfields, not assumed — see the necessity lemmas below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}